---
import ProseLayout from '@/layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import { ROUTES } from '@/config/site';
const meta = {
  title: 'Editorial Policy',
  description:
    'How Would You Rather Questions selects, categorizes, reviews and retires questions.',
  path: ROUTES.editorialPolicy,
};
---

<ProseLayout meta={meta} heading="Editorial Policy">
  <h2>Selection</h2>
  <p>
    Every question must offer two genuinely different options, be understandable without extra
    context, and suit at least one category's audience.
  </p>
  <h2>Category suitability</h2>
  <p>
    Content suitability is controlled through category assignment. Kids, family, school and work
    categories contain only clean material. Mature categories are suggestive at most and never
    graphic. A question is never assigned to both a mature and a child-safe category.
  </p>
  <h2>Submissions</h2>
  <p>
    We review question ideas sent by email. We may edit, decline or re-categorize them. We do not
    publish personal information about people who send us questions.
  </p>
  <h2>Corrections and removals</h2>
  <p>
    Report problems via the <a href={ROUTES.contact}>contact page</a>. Retired questions are
    archived rather than deleted so existing share links show a helpful notice.
  </p>
  <h2>Trademarks</h2>
  <p>
    References to third-party names (for example themed collections) are descriptive only and imply
    no affiliation, sponsorship or endorsement.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
